You can disable the common scaling factor using scaled y ticks = false
in the axis options. This will lead to each individual tick label being displayed in scientific notation, which you can suppress by also using y tick label style={/pgf/number format/fixed}
(see section "4.18.1 All Supported Styles" of the PGFplots Manual for the other options of formatting the numbers).

\documentclass{minimal}
\usepackage{pgfplots}

\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
scaled y ticks = false,
y tick label style={/pgf/number format/fixed,
/pgf/number format/1000 sep = \thinspace % Optional if you want to replace comma as the 1000 separator
}]
\addplot coordinates {
(100,200001)
(200,200003)
(300,200005)
};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

\end{document}

